cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its findings, please cite this repository."
title: "Few-Shot Detection of Aspilanta on Yellow Sticky Traps"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-12"
authors:
  - family-names: "Abdul Malick"
    given-names: "Nawfal"
    email: "nawfal.abdulmalick@usi.ch"
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Nawfal-AI/aspilanta-fewshot-detection"
url: "https://github.com/Nawfal-AI/aspilanta-fewshot-detection"
abstract: >-
  A few-shot object detection pipeline for rare agricultural pests, combining
  copy-paste synthetic compositing, staged YOLOv8s transfer learning, and a
  frozen-CLIP prototype filter. Trained from 44 real target cutouts.
  Achieves AP@50 = 0.981 on the target-domain validation set.
keywords:
  - few-shot object detection
  - synthetic data
  - precision agriculture
  - pest monitoring
  - YOLOv8
  - CLIP
  - computer vision
